{"v":1,"accession":"PRJEB36651","title":"Community composition of various biosolids obtained from german wastewater treatment plants.","description":"Soil fertilization with biosolids from wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs) inherits the risk of disseminating resistance genes (RGs), mobile genetic elements (MGEs) and potentially selective pollutants (antibiotics [ABs], heavy metals, biocides) into soil. However, only few data are available on the parallel analysis of biosolid pollutant contents and RG/MGE abundances. In present study, total community (TC)-DNA of biosolids from 12 WWTPs (one large-scale and 11 small-/middle-scale) was analyzed for the abundance of RGs and MGEs via quantitative real-time PCR or PCR-Southern blot hybridization and concentrations of heavy metals, ABs and the biocides triclosan (TCS), triclocarban (TCC) and quaternary ammonium compounds were determined, together with prokaryotic community.","center":"DTU Bioengineering","data_type":"Other","submission_date":"2020/05/31 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMEA6529085","WWTP_AIII-1","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,2018,"DE",null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"Germany",null,null,null,null,"urban context stated at BioProject level only"],["SAMEA6529086","WWTP_AIII-2","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,2018,"DE",null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"Germany",null,null,null,null,"urban context stated at BioProject level only"],["SAMEA6529087","WWTP_AIII-3","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,2019,"DE",null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"Germany",null,null,null,null,"urban context stated at BioProject level only"],["SAMEA6529088","WWTP_AIII-4","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,2020,"DE",null,null,n